    "body": "### Problem\n\nMotion that are result of `<Cmd>...<CR>` mapping are not followed during multicursor.\n\nPossibly related: #41634, #41646\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim --clean -- Makefile` (from the root of this repo)\n2. Do one of:\n    2.1. `:nnoremap ^ <Cmd>normal! 0^<CR>`\n    2.2. `:lua move = function() vim.api.nvim_win_set_cursor(0, { vim.fn.line('.'), 0 }) end` and `nnoremap ^ <Cmd>lua move()<CR>`.\n3. Type `vip` - `Q` to start multicursor with following mode.\n4. Press `$` - cursors follow to the end of line.\n5. Press `^` - only the primary cursor moves.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nMotions that are result of mappings are followed during multicursor.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1499+gb51a0b2dcc\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nNo, doesn't have this functionality\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nEndeavourOS Linux x86_64, 7.1.11-arch1-1\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nGhostty 1.3.1-arch2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-ghostty\n\n### Installation\n\nAppimage and from source",
